  <section>
    <h2>A practice built across disciplines</h2>
    <p>
      My work has moved between graphic design, websites, agency leadership and
      hands-on production. The common thread is translating an idea into
      something that works for someone else.
    </p>
    <p>
      Co-founding In10tion meant moving between design, development and client
      conversations. At We Are Coast, interface work sat alongside custom
      websites, infrastructure and the systems that helped the studio deliver.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Getting closer to the product</h2>
    <p>
      With Flowforest, that experience is coming together around independent
      products. Runway, Flare and Slate explore different ways to capture and
      work with ideas: files, voice and handwriting.
    </p>
    <p>
      Agentic development is part of how I’m building them. It brings more of
      the implementation within reach of the design process, while leaving the
      product decisions, trade-offs and responsibility with me.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>A working journal</h2>
    <p>
      This space follows the work as it develops: the decisions, interface
      studies and things learned by making. These products are still in
      progress. That makes this a useful place to show how they take shape.
    </p>
  </section>
